00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.980
I'm talking today about

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.860
two songs which were recorded by an

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.789
amateur folk singer, Jack Milstein,

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:45.790
a Polish Jew.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.370
He served in the Polish Army.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.279
He was born in 1913.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.409
So he served in the Polish Army

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.319
in the late 20s

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.090
and early 30s.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.946
This was a difficult
time, I think, for Jews

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.840
in the Polish army, the NCOs,

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.149
the officers, indeed, the men were not

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.669
that sympathetic towards Jewish

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.929
recruits, particularly ones who

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.529
were not that acculturated.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.908
Most times speaks, sings his two

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.129
songs in Polish.

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.729
I mean, he has a slight accent in Polish,

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.039
but his Polish is clearly good and he has

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.770
no problems either recording

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:27.378
in Polish or indeed presumably speaking in

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:28.480
Polish.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.689
The first song is

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:34.059
a song about, so-called humorous

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.360
song, mocking Jewish recruits.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.149
Instead of loading his gun

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.399
with bullets, the Jewish recruit

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.674
loads his gun with onions.

00:11:43.247 --> 00:11:44.247
Of course onions and

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:48.059
Jews, like garlic and Jews, is one of those

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.710
East European tropes.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.192
And not only does he load his gun with

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.962
onions, but he shoots at his

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.509
wife and his wife is called not

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.189
kobieta, but kobita, the women.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.250
It's a rather

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.270
lower class Polish expression.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.469
The other song he sings is a

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.660
love song and it's a rather

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.820
attractive song.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.229
I mean, I don't see it as being humorous or

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.020
in any sense anti-Jewish.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.500
And what it reflects, in my view, is

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.350
the degree to which Polish popular culture

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.460
had penetrated into the Jewish

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.390
world in the 1920s and the 1930s,

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.480
although particularly after 1935,

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.900
antisemitism increased in Poland.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.940
And indeed in the early years of the

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.862
Pilsudski regime, after Pilsudski

00:12:35.272 --> 00:12:36.492
took power in May

00:12:37.512 --> 00:12:39.191
1926, the government

00:12:39.822 --> 00:12:42.162
attempted to reach an understanding with

00:12:42.312 --> 00:12:44.321
the various national minorities and indeed

00:12:44.322 --> 00:12:46.181
with the Jews. And until the death of

00:12:46.602 --> 00:12:48.762
General Pilsudski in May 1935,

00:12:48.942 --> 00:12:50.515
Jews felt relatively comfortable.

00:12:50.516 --> 00:12:52.500
But throughout this

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.780
period, in the period when the

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.430
Jewish situation was relatively good

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.220
after 1926 and as it deteriorated

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.439
first under the impact of the Great

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.406
Depression and then after the death of

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.731
Marshal Pilsudski when a section of the

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.609
government camp attempted to strengthen

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.829
its position by making common

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.496
cause with the antisemitic part of

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:16.100
the Polish right, there

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:18.229
was a high degree of acculturation taking

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.629
place. So along with the

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.609
deterioration of the situation of the Jews,

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.099
they went and adopted the Polish language.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.320
And I think this is reflected

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.599
in Milstein's songs.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.660
He sings songs in Polish.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.180
He has no problem singing these songs

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:36.609
in Polish, and he's clearly

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:38.799
quite comfortable singing them in Polish.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.049
So they reflect, on the one hand, the

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.170
ambivalent position of the Jews, relatively

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.580
stable in the late 1920s and early

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:49.119
1930s when Milstein is serving

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.639
in the Polish army, deteriorating

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.959
after 1935.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.719
But also it reflects the growing

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:57.310
acculturation of Jews.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.920
And one element in this, which

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.170
perhaps is linked with these songs

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.960
is the fact that Polish popular culture,

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.139
Polish popular music, Polish songs

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.410
were an area where

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.589
Jews were extremely

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.830
active.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.091
Jews were among the people who produced

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:20.560
jazz, Wlast and

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.680
the other major Jewish singers.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.840
These were people who were

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.359
accepted on the larger Polish scene.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:30.310
And as in the United States,

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.920
the Polish equivalent of Tin Pan Alley

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.229
had a heavily Jewish

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.160
component.

